<title>NETHERLANDS: Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stock levels.</title>
<headline>Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stock levels.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oil product inventories held in independent tankage in the Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp area were estimated to be at the following levels currently, a week ago and a year ago, industry sources said.</p>
<p>All figures in thousands of tonnes:</p>
<p>			 7/5/97		   1/5/97		9/5/96</p>
<p>    Gasoline	625-650			650		   400</p>
<p>    Naphtha	     125		  100-125		    50</p>
<p>    Gas oil	   1,700		    1,650		 1,500</p>
<p>    Fuel oil	350-375			400	     300-325</p>
<p>    Jet kero	     10			 10		 10-20</p>
<p>Stock levels were broadly balanced.</p>
<p>Gasoline stocks were replenished with ARA-produced product, but barges took other material to Germany.</p>
<p>Naphtha stocks rose slightly, though little product arrived.</p>
<p>Gas oil stocks were up as incoming cargoes outweighed barge departures down the Rhine and into France.</p>
<p>Fuel oil stocks dipped as straight-run product moved into Germany and the bunker market took some, but not much, cracked material.</p>
<p>Jet fuel stocks barely changed.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam Newsroom, +31 20 504 5004</p>
</text>
